data_InP_zincblende_Haruna_et_al_1987

_audit_creation_method
;
Reconstructed project reference for room-temperature zincblende InP.

The cubic lattice parameter used in this project is a = 5.8688 Angstrom
at approximately 300 K.

This is the rounded representation of the standard room-temperature
lattice parameter a = 5.86875 Angstrom reported in established InP
structural-property literature.

Experimental temperature-dependent lattice measurements were reported by:

K. Haruna, H. Maeta, K. Ohashi and T. Koike,
"The thermal expansion coefficient and Gruneisen parameter of InP
crystal at low temperatures",
Journal of Physics C: Solid State Physics 20, 5275-5279 (1987).
DOI: 10.1088/0022-3719/20/32/013

Haruna et al. measured the InP lattice constant over the range
4.2-300 K using the precision X-ray Bond method.

The crystallographic model is zincblende InP, space group F-43m
(No. 216), represented by the symmetry-inequivalent In and P sites.

This file is a reconstructed project reference and is not an original
deposited experimental CIF.
;

